===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hoist]] with, or as if with, a derrick.
# {{lb|en|transitive|baseball|informal}} To [[remove]] (a [[pitcher]]).
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Ray Robinson|title=High and Tight
|passage=Stinky, who had batted a bit over .200 with scant power (two home runs in 66 games in 1933), was being '''derricked''' by Navin.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2014|author=Addie Joss; Gary Mitchem|title=Addie Joss on Baseball|page=96
|passage=As a rule, when the twirler is '''derricked''', it is because the members of the opposition are beginning to take undue familiarity with his offerings. But this is not always the reason.}}

